# LiNKtrend Ecosystem Master Rule

Cursor is the architecture and integration IDE for the LiNKtrend AI Agent Ecosystem. Codex, Antigravity, Gemini/Kimi, and other agents are bounded workers operating through `LiNKdev/` programs and issues.

Repository files, Git history, `LiNKdev/` documents, and committed implementation files are the source of truth. Do not rely on chat memory, IDE memory, or unstated assumptions. Legacy `.ai-swarm/` is archived at `Archive/.ai-swarm-legacy/`.

Before coding, read in this order:

1. `.cursor/rules/`
2. `LiNKdev/skills/SKILLS_CATALOG.md` (IDE routing: `.cursor/skills/SKILLS_CATALOG.md`)
3. `LiNKdev/command-center/ARCHITECT_REVIEW_REPORT.md` if present
4. `docs/architecture/repo-architecture-target.md`
5. `docs/architecture/system-completion-targets.md`
6. `LiNKdev/command-center/MASTER_PLAN.md`
7. `LiNKdev/command-center/ARCHITECTURE_RULES.md`
8. `LiNKdev/command-center/CONTRACTS_MVO.md`
9. `LiNKdev/command-center/REPO_INVENTORY.md`
10. `LiNKdev/command-center/DECISIONS.md`
11. the active issue under `LiNKdev/programs/<program>/issues/`

Use `LiNKdev/skills/SKILLS_CATALOG.md` for progressive disclosure: select the skills, MCP servers, and plugin references relevant to the task before opening full skill bodies or tool descriptors. Do not bulk-load every skill file.

If `LiNKdev/` is missing, bootstrap from `LiNKdev/install/` first. Do not implement application code before the command center exists.

The first MVO is the LinkSites / WebsiteFactory lead-to-preview-site flow.

The development posture is reuse-first: inspect active and archived repos before creating new implementation.

New work must use the canonical post-cleanup folders: `LiNKaios/`, `LiNKbrain/`, `LiNKskills/`, `LiNKautowork/`, `LiNKbot/`, `LiNKguard/`, and `modules/`. Do not create new work under legacy `plugins/vertical` or moved `apps/*` runtime paths.

For module work, start in the module folder and maintain one canonical workflow map there. The module workflow map is the readable source of truth; other planes implement referenced parts through their own ownership folders.
